\label{lem:r-1}Let $m> 0$, $\alpha\geqslant 5$ and let $g:[0,\infty)\to [0,\infty)$ be a log-concave
function with finite positive integral. Let $\varrho_{\alpha m}:=\sup\{r>0:g(r)\geqslant e^{-\alpha m}g(0)\}$. Then,
$$\int_0^{\varrho_{\alpha m}}r^{m}g(r)\,dr\geqslant\left(1-e^{-\alpha m/4}\right)\int_0^{\infty}r^{m}g(r)\,dr.$$

\label{prop:1}There exists $t_0\geqslant 1$ such that, for every centered log-concave probability measure $\mu $ on ${\mathbb R}^n$ and 
every $s\geqslant t\geqslant t_0$,
\begin{equation*}Z_t^+(\mu) \subseteq \left(1+\frac{2\ln s}{s}\right)B_s(\mu).\end{equation*}
